            "body": "`needs_temp` seems misleading. The result may or may not be in a temp, the question is more if it can be reused or not.\n\nI think we can do without the flag.\n```suggestion\n        last_result = args[0]\n        first_result_ref = result_ref = cascaded_nodes[0]\n        for arg_node in cascaded_nodes[1:]:\n```",
            "commit_id": "c974d868500eded851c774bdc82530f2ac349e0a",
            "copilot_code_review_severity": null,
            "copilot_code_review_sources": [],
            "created_at": "2026-11-19T08:16:24Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -2107,11 +2107,14 @@ def _optimise_min_max(self, node, args, operator):\n                 # leave this to Python\n                 return node\n \n-        cascaded_nodes = list(map(UtilNodes.ResultRefNode, args[1:]))\n-\n-        last_result = args[0]\n-        for arg_node in cascaded_nodes:\n-            result_ref = UtilNodes.ResultRefNode(last_result)\n+        # Evaluate all arguments from left to right before comparing them.\n+        cascaded_nodes = list(map(UtilNodes.ResultRefNode, args))\n+\n+        last_result = cascaded_nodes[0]\n+        for arg_node in cascaded_nodes[1:]:\n+            # The first argument is already in a temp, later results are not.\n+            needs_temp = last_result is not cascaded_nodes[0]\n+            result_ref = UtilNodes.ResultRefNode(last_result) if needs_temp else last_result",
